        "comments": "Chromosomes 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 have been assembled into a single sequence each. However, they had to be split into two pieces because the chromosome length exceeds the technical limit of roughly 2.14 billion base pairs. The chromosomes are separated at the centromere.\n\nThis is the maternal pseudohaplotype assembly created from the genome sequence of the F1 female progeny (isolate Amex_F1_6; BioSample SAMN41071122) of a cross between a female Ambystoma mexicanum (isolate Mex_15411; BioSample SAMN43142723) and male Ambystoma tigrinum (isolate Tig_M23; BioSample SAMN43142724).",
